# Backend (`apps/backend`)

AdonisJS 7 API app. **Follow [AdonisJS official folder structure](https://docs.adonisjs.com/guides/getting-started/folder-structure) and Ace naming generators** — do not apply Nest `dot.role` from `backend.mdc` (`apps/api`).

SSOT for layout/names: Adonis docs + `node ace make:*`. Placement vs monorepo packages: `layering` + `structure` (Adonis `app/**` is a **framework tree** exception to flat-by-default).

## Official directory layout (keep)

```text
apps/backend/
├── app/                 # domain logic
│   ├── controllers/
│   ├── exceptions/
│   ├── mails/
│   ├── middleware/
│   ├── models/
│   ├── services/        # create when needed
│   ├── transformers/
│   └── validators/
├── bin/                 # server / console / test entrypoints
├── config/              # app + package config
├── database/            # migrations, schema.ts, schema_rules.ts, seeders, factories
├── providers/
├── start/               # env, kernel, routes, validators boot
├── tests/               # unit / functional + bootstrap.ts (Japa)
├── ace.js
├── adonisrc.ts
└── package.json
```

- Prefer adding folders **under `app/`** when organizing domain code (official guidance).
- Do **not** invent Nest-style `src/modules/<domain>/` or `src/common/` here.
- Commit `.adonisjs/` (generated client/server types); required for `#generated/*` and CI.
- Ignore `tmp/` (and do not ship sqlite files under `tmp/`).

## Official naming (Ace generators)

Use **`node ace make:*`** so names stay consistent with the framework.

| Artifact | File | Class / export | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Controller | `posts_controller.ts` (plural + `_controller`) | `PostsController` | `make:controller posts` |
| Middleware | `body_parser_middleware.ts` (singular + `_middleware`) | `BodyParserMiddleware` | `make:middleware` |
| Model | `user.ts` / `post.ts` (singular) | `User` / `Post` | `make:model Post`; table `posts` via Lucid |
| Validator | `user.ts` / `post.ts` (singular, by resource) | exported Vine schemas | `make:validator`; one file may hold create/update |
| Provider | `app_provider.ts` (snake_case) | — | `make:provider` |
| Migration | `*_create_posts_table.ts` | — | `make:migration` / `make:model -m` |
| DB columns | `snake_case` in SQL | `camelCase` on models | Lucid maps automatically |

**Do not** rename to Nest `auth.controller.ts` / kebab `mail-cooldown.service.ts` inside this app.

Subpath imports use package `#` aliases (`#controllers/*`, `#models/*`, …) as defined in `package.json` `imports` — not `@/` and not Nest relative `.js` style from `apps/api`.

## Stack (this app)

| Concern | Choice |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP / DI / lifecycle | `@adonisjs/core` |
| ORM | Lucid (`@adonisjs/lucid`) — schema lives under `database/` |
| Auth | `@adonisjs/auth` access tokens (`api` guard) |
| Mail | `@adonisjs/mail` (Resend) + Edge/`BaseMail` |
| Validation | VineJS |
| Redis | `@adonisjs/redis` |
| Tests | Japa |
| Env | `start/env.ts` (`Env.create`) |

Persistence for **this** app is Lucid — do not import `@elynd/db` / Drizzle into `apps/backend` unless an explicit dual-read decision is documented.

## Env (Compose-aligned)

Validate in `start/env.ts`. Typical local Compose mapping:

- Postgres host port **5433** → `DB_HOST` / `DB_PORT` / `DB_USER` / `DB_PASSWORD` / `DB_DATABASE`
- Redis host port **6380** → `REDIS_HOST` / `REDIS_PORT`

Prefer dedicated DB name for Adonis while Nest still shares Compose (avoid clobbering Better Auth tables).

## Routes & HTTP

- Register routes in `start/routes.ts`; middleware stacks in `start/kernel.ts`.
- Prefer thin controllers; put non-trivial rules in `app/services` (create via Ace when 2+ call sites or clear SRP need).
- API JSON shaping: keep starter `providers/api_provider.ts` serialize wrap unless product changes the contract.

## Scaffolding

```bash
node ace make:controller posts
node ace make:model Post -m
node ace make:validator user
node ace make:middleware guest
node ace make:provider app
```

Prefer Ace over hand-creating differently named files.

## Out of scope here

- Nest `apps/api` → see `backend.mdc`
- Next `apps/web` → see `frontend.mdc`
- OpenAPI / Apifox — deferred until product asks
